Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(graph):=20plugins=20on=20a=20send=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20a=20wet=20branch=20between=20the=20tap=20and=20its?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20level?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A BridgeTapSource may expose a mini-chain (getTapChain) and a head step
(processTapHead). When the chain holds an enabled plugin the builder shares
the tapped node between the tap (dry, untouched) and a wet branch: head node,
the chain's nodes, a priming gag; the tap's age is the wet's latency. Without
a chain the graph is the previous one, node for node.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
